ENTRY            32938   20260914   20261124   20261124       3224
SUBENT        32938001   20260914   20261124   20261124       3224
BIB                 14         35
TITLE      Cross-sections for formation of 73Ga through
            natGe(n,x)73Ga reaction induced by d-T neutrons
AUTHOR     (Junhua Luo, Long He, Liang Zhou, Li Jiang)
INSTITUTE  (3CPRHXU,3CPRNPC)
           (3CPRCPR) Department of Basic Science, Lanzhou
            Institute of Technology, Lanzhou
REFERENCE  (J,RPC,227,112384,2025)
           #doi:10.1016/j.radphyschem.2024.112384
SAMPLE     Each sample was machined with Ge as a Phi = 20 mm
            diameter disc (thickness ~1 mm, purity 99.999%).
            Five such samples were prepared for neutron
            irradiation, each with a mass of about 1.6 g.
FACILITY   (NGEN,3CPRNPC) K-400 neutron generator
INC-SOURCE (D-T) The thickness of the tritium-titanium (T-Ti)
            target was 2.65 mg/cm2, the current of the incident
            deuterium beam causing the nuclear reaction T(d,n)
            4He was 240 uA, the average deuterium beam energy was
            135 keV, and the neutron yields remained in the about
            4 to 5 E10 n/s range.
INC-SPECT  (EN-RSL-HW) Spread estimated by the distance from
            the sample to the target and the solid angle of
            the sample.
METHOD     (ACTIV) The sample was irradiated for 2 h, and cooled
            for 1.6 - 2.3 h. A typical spectrum of the measured
            germanium sample is cooling time 1.73 h, measurement
            live time 996.54 s.
DETECTOR   (HPGE) A high-purity germanium (HPGe) detector type
            from ORTEC (model GEM 60P, crystal diameter: 70.1 mm,
            crystal length: 72.3 mm, made in U.S.A.). The energy
            resolution of the detector was 1.69 keV at 1332 keV
            of 60Co, and its relative efficiency was about 68%.
MONITOR    (13-AL-27(N,A)11-NA-24,,SIG)
DECAY-MON  (11-NA-24,14.997HR,DG,1368.6,1.00)
MONIT-REF  (,,3,IRDFF-II,,2020)
HISTORY    (20260914C) Compiled by Xi Tao (CNDC)
ENDBIB              35
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           38
